 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Ratings",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Continuous drain current is 10 A at a 25 °C case and 6.3 A at 100 °C with 10 V of gate drive; power dissipation of 125 W at 25 °C falls by 1.0 W for each °C above it. Fig. 9 gives the allowed drain current against case temperature, reaching zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Avalanche",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The part is rated for a single avalanche pulse of 520 mJ (starting at TJ = 25 °C, 10 A, 9.1 mH from 50 V) and for repeated avalanche at 10 A and 13 mJ per pulse, with the pulse length limited by junction temperature. Fig. 12c shows how the allowed single-pulse energy shrinks as the starting junction temperature rises, for 4.5 A, 5.3 A and 10 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The integral diode carries 10 A continuous and 40 A pulsed, drops at most 2.0 V at 10 A, and recovers in 370 ns typical (790 ns max) with 3.8 µC typical stored charge at 100 A/µs. After recovery the drain may rise at up to 4.0 V/ns for ISD ≤ 10 A and dI/dt ≤ 120 A/µs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The threshold falls between 2.0 V and 4.0 V; the on-resistance limit of 0.55 Ω holds at 10 V of drive. Taking the gate from 0 to 10 V at 320 V and 10 A needs up to 63 nC in all, up to 9.0 nC of it gate-source charge and up to 32 nC gate-drain charge. The internal gate resistance lies between 0.8 Ω and 5.9 Ω. On-resistance roughly doubles from 25 °C to 125 °C (Fig. 4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mounting",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The TO-220AB is fastened with a 6-32 or M3 screw at up to 10 lbf·in (1.1 N·m). Leads may see a peak of 300 °C for 10 s, measured 1.6 mm from the case. A flat, greased mounting surface adds 0.50 °C/W typical between case and heatsink."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Manufacturing",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The part may come from any of several qualified Vishay sites; reliability data cover all of them combined."
  }
 ]
